The contract implements a pension system but contains a critical vulnerability in its update authorization logic.

### Vulnerability: Arbitrary update
### Explanation: The contract improperly handles application updates by allowing the company to update any aspect of the application logic rather than restricting updates to specific, authorized pension-related parameters. This could allow malicious updates to the entire contract logic.
### Risk: Critical - Allows complete takeover of the pension system by replacing its core logic.
